#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# time_series

#% text
# `time_series(values, times)`: values at times. Also `time_series([[t, v], ...])`, `time_series(values)` (times 0, 1, ...) and `time_series(values, [t0, t1])` (times spaced evenly from t0 to t1); `ts("Values")`, `ts("Times")`, `ts("Path")`, `ts("FirstValue")`, `ts("LastValue")`, `ts("FirstTime")`, `ts("LastTime")`, `ts("Duration")`, `ts("Length")`; `mean`, `median`, `variance`, `std_dev` act on the values

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
ts = time_series([5, 6, 8])

#% cell
ts("Path")
#% output
#= [[0, 5], [1, 6], [2, 8]]

#% cell
time_series([1, 2, 3], [10, 20])
#% output
#= time_series([1, 2, 3], [10, 15, 20])

#% cell
mean(ts)
#% output
#= 19/3

